WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.412
This is Coding Exercise 1 for Assignment 3 The goal
is to

00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:08.712
practice a basic SELECT statement and sorting You
need to return three

00:00:08.738 --> 00:00:13.712
columns from the patients table MRN full name and
age Then sort

00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:17.950
the rows from oldest to youngest Start with the
SELECT keyword and

00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:22.575
list the three columns separated by commas The FROM
clause is already

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:26.788
pointing to the patients table Then add an ORDER BY
clause using

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.362
age Because oldest should come first use descending
order Before

00:00:32.388 --> 00:00:35.375
you click Run and Check read the query as a sentence
show

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.800
MRN full name and age from patients and order the
result by

00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:43.100
age from highest to lowest When the query runs
inspect the output

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:47.388
even if the checker says the exercise is correct The
age values

00:00:47.412 --> 00:00:50.850
should decrease as you move down the result If you
get a

00:00:50.862 --> 00:00:54.300
syntax error look for common issues such as a
missing comma a

00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:58.825
missing column name or an incomplete ORDER BY clause
Remember that your

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.888
work is saved in the current browser You can reset
the starter

00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:06.825
code if needed but try to repair your own query
first The

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:10.125
purpose of the exercise is to build confidence
reading and writing a

00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:11.450
small complete statement
